# Tenant inspection notices

When a resident forwards or reports an upcoming housing inspection (HABC annual schedule, date change, etc.), treat it as **`inspection_notice`** — not `maintenance_new`.

## Model

| Piece | Value |
|---|---|
| `inspection_reports.letter_type` | `tenant_notice` |
| Deficiencies / checklist WOs | **none** — notice stands alone |
| Source screenshot | `inspection_source_documents` → `source_document_id` |
| Related repairs | **Separate** maintenance tickets; at most a plain-text timing note (`Timing note: ahead of 10/8 HABC inspection.`) — **no** `inspection_report_id` |
| PM Compliance | `preventive_maintenance_tasks` via `planStandaloneInspectionPmComplianceTask` (due on inspection date) |

## Flow

1. Classify `inspection_notice` before repair keywords swallow the thread.
2. `ensureTenantInspectionNoticeReport` creates/reuses an open notice row for the unit + date (source doc when media is present) and ensures a PM Compliance row.
3. Repairs in the same message continue as **standalone** work orders. Do not attach them as checklist items under the inspection.

## Distinct from landlord HQS letters

| | Landlord HQS letter | Tenant notice |
|---|---|---|
| Who | Landlord MMS | Resident SMS |
| Confirm | YES before create | Create on notice |
| Checklist | Fail items → `inspection_report_id` WOs (N-of-M when **>1**) | No linked WOs |
| `letter_type` | `standard_fail` / `hap_abatement` | `tenant_notice` |
| Active Tasks | Existing grouped visit card only | Standalone card (`inspection_notice_task`) |

## Active Tasks — standalone card (zero-checklist only)

Standalone Active Tasks cards exist because **tenant notices have no checklist** to anchor an N-of-M visit card — not because of which channel submitted them. Same treatment for manual admin entry (or any path) when itemized fail counts are zero.

| Record | Active Tasks |
|---|---|
| `tenant_notice` (0 itemized fails) | Standalone card: “[Letter type] inspection — [date]”, next step **Prepare for inspection** |
| Unknown / manual with `emergency_item_count + standard_item_count === 0` | Same standalone card |
| `standard_fail` / `hap_abatement` (HQS) | **No** standalone card — existing N-of-M visit card only (avoid duplicate) |

Helpers: `shouldShowStandaloneInspectionActiveTask` / `loadStandaloneInspectionTaskRows`. Synthetic row id `inspection-report:{uuid}`.

Creating or viewing the inspection task must **never** auto-link, gate, or absorb work orders.

## Do not

- Route the notice into an open pest/repair ticket
- Put the HABC screenshot on a repair WO’s `photo_paths` — it belongs on the inspection source document
- Set `inspection_report_id` / shared due_at / visit-card membership from a tenant notice onto unrelated repairs
- Add a second Active Tasks card for HQS letters that already have the N-of-M visit group
- Invent a parallel inspection or compliance product — reuse `inspection_reports` + `preventive_maintenance_tasks`

## Future (architecture)

Intent classification is still an expanding set of special-case rules (water-outage vocab, multi-issue split, recurring false-positives, inspection notices absorbed into repairs). Schedule a dedicated review of the classification architecture itself rather than another one-off per symptom.
